WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.370
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:07.710
I have a question for you, when was the last
time you watched the news and didn't see bad

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.890
news.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:13.370
When did you least read a headline that read
"Sorry folks, no news today because all is

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.929
fine and dandy in the world".

00:00:14.929 --> 00:00:23.000
Apart from that one day, on 18th April 1930
when there was no news, so they simply played

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.289
piano music for 15 minutes instead of the
usual news bulletin.

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:29.700
Yes that actually happened.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.480
It's easy to believe that we're all doomed.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:39.379
With the Gaza Strip, ISIS, Ebola, countless
civil wars, school shootings, killer cops

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:43.159
and a handful of highly questionable world
leaders.

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:50.190
It seems that every year the world is falling
deeper and deeper into a pit of hatred, deceit,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.510
murder, war, terrorism and despair.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:01:01.250
One could easily believe that the world is
more dangerous than it has ever been and only

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.690
getting more so.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.340
But what's the truth?

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.810
Are things getting better or worse?

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:11.290
What does the outlook look like for the future
of mankind?

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:19.100
To find out we need to do one very important
thing, completely ignore every news source

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.700
in the world.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:27.350
You see, there is an intrinsic problem with
news, they only report the bad news and the

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.470
worse the news is the higher billing it receives.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:35.080
Front page headlines are reserved for only
the most miserable events that unfold around

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.530
the world each day.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:43.660
Whether it be TV news, tabloids or even social
media, news outlets need to attract large

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.870
numbers of viewers or they will inevitably
fail.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:53.550
So naturally the most compelling stories are
chosen to make headlines.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.990
Well, it makes sense doesn't it?

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:03.409
By its very definition news would not be news
if it was not something out of the ordinary.

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:07.950
Although it's nice to hear, reporting that
millions of cars arrived safely at their destinations

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:13.360
this week is not news, but reporting a fatal
collision is.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.530
And because news only reports the bad events
it gives the majority of people the impression

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:24.520
that these awful events are far more likely
to occur than they actually do.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.130
Headlines would have us believe that terrorists
are waiting for us, planning their next attack

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:32.180
around every corner, at every airport or transportation
system.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:38.530
A data scientist recently calculated the odds
of a person dying in a terrorist attack.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:44.330
He concluded that your chances are 1 in 25
million.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:52.251
Let me put that into perspective, your chance
of dying in the bathtub is 1 in 680,000, so

00:02:52.251 --> 00:02:57.810
you're 36 times more likely to die in the
tub than at the hands of a terrorist.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:04.940
Also, you're 2.5 times more likely to become
a president and 2 times more likely to become

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.099
an astronaut, than to die in a terrorist attack.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:15.450
Of course this is no solace to the unfortunate
victims of such attacks but it just goes to

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:21.990
demonstrate how news headlines can artificially
inflate our worries and negative expectations

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.660
of the World.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:28.120
But the reality is really rather different.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:34.810
What if, despite everything you've heard and
everything you've read, I told you, that the

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:41.000
world is more peaceful right now than ever
before.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.500
Many experts, including German economist Max
Roser have said that we are currently living

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:51.330
in the most peaceful period of our species'
existence.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:58.069
Max Roser of Oxford University runs the website
Our World in Data and this astonishing chart

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:05.670
shows the global deaths in conflicts per 100,000
people, every year since 1400.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:12.170
The past 15 years have seen a rapid and substantial
drop in conflict deaths worldwide.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:19.380
But that's just in war, what about on our
streets, what about theft, murder and rape?

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:26.020
Well, this graph shows the homicide rates
per 100,000 people in various European regions

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:31.070
between the year 1300 and today, that's quite
a decline.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:35.840
But that goes all the way back to the middle
ages when your best friend would bash your

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.300
head in for a leg of lamb.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.090
How about over the past couple of decades?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:47.120
This graph shows the rates of robbery, homicide
and vehicle theft across the G7 countries

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:55.270
between 1995 and 2010, all three crimes have
reduced significantly.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.960
But hold on, what about terrorism?

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:03.830
Surely that's becoming more prevalent each
year, not a month goes by when we don't hear

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.770
about an awful attack somewhere around the
World.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:11.820
Yes, it's true that jihadist terrorism has
increased over the past two decades.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:18.710
But overall, if we take every event of terrorism
from the past 50 years, the frequency of attacks

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:28.710
has dropped significantly, especially over
the past decade, according Our World in Data

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:35.780
in 2006 there were 6,660 counts of terrorism
worldwide, by 2009 that had dropped to just

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.600
560.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:43.150
And the number of deaths from terrorism has
dropped also.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:47.860
When we take all these factors and put them
together it creates an interesting picture

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:54.020
as to what is happening with World peace and
that's exactly what the institute for economics

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.420
and peace has done.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:02.590
Every year the Sydney-based research firm
analyses thousands of bits of data from every

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:10.160
country and produces a peace score and a ranking
for every country on Earth, called the Global

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.710
Peace Index.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:18.690
In their latest, 2017 index the five most
peaceful countries on Earth are Iceland, New

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:22.720
Zealand, Portugal, Austria and Denmark.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:28.630
And the least peaceful are Syria, Afghanistan,
Iraq, South Sudan and Yemen.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:35.360
But if you look at the change in each country's
peace index over the past 10 years something

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:42.180
strange has happened which explains why overall
the world is becoming less violent whilst

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:46.830
the newspapers are doing the opposite and
only filling up with more violence.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.300
The peace gap is widening.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:56.350
The authors of the Global Peace Index have
stated that over the past ten years 81 countries

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:02.960
that were already peaceful, have only become
more peaceful, yet 79 countries that were

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:08.850
already un-peaceful have become even less
peaceful.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:14.310
According to the Global Peace Index Europe
is the most peaceful region in the World,

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:22.139
and every year since the index began, European
countries have only got more and more peaceful

00:07:22.139 --> 00:07:27.780
each year, except for France which has seen
a slight drop in its rankings due to the recent

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.180
terrorist attacks in the country.

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:35.949
However, the publishers of the study have
said that today most European countries are

00:07:35.949 --> 00:07:41.850
now more peaceful than they have ever been
in recorded history.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:47.880
Conversely, the world's least peaceful regions,
the Middle East and North Africa, have only

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:52.940
got less peaceful each and every year and
are now less peaceful than ever.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:57.780
But as always, there is one developed country
that has bucked the trend of increased peace

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:58.930
amongst its peers.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:05.930
Not only has the United States of America
dropped its ranking every year but its peace

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:12.550
index has also fallen faster than any other
major developed country.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:23.199
In 2015 the US was ranked 94 out of 163 countries,
in 2016 it was ranked 103 and this year it

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:31.410
fell again to 114 out of 163 countries, a
rapid drop which the researchers attribute

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:37.419
in part to increased political instability
and divide in recent years.

00:08:37.419 --> 00:08:43.760
But how did Iceland get to be number one on
the list?

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:49.450
Not only that, Iceland has always been number
one, for as long as the Global Peace Index

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:54.460
has existed, Iceland has been ranked the most
peaceful country on Earth.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.430
And the reason behind it is fascinating.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.920
Iceland isn't the world's most peaceful place
because of the country's remoteness and its

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:04.350
beautiful scenery, although it certainly helps.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.300
Iceland is so peaceful because it has to be.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:13.149
Iceland is one of the harshest environments
on the planet and for hundreds of years the

00:09:13.149 --> 00:09:19.580
natives have had to take unusual steps to
survive the bitterly cold, unforgiving tundra.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:24.430
If they spent all their time fighting one
another they would have perished to the elements,

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:30.020
so instead they had to work together to survive
mother nature.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:35.670
Throughout the ages it has been perfectly
acceptable and quite common in Icelandic culture

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:42.750
to enter someone's house, even if you have
never met them and even if they're not home,

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:47.540
and make yourself a cup of tea in their kitchen,
to warm yourself up.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:52.970
That's a level of trust and community that
would be completely unfathomable for citizens

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:54.529
of most other countries.

00:09:54.529 --> 00:10:01.100
But it was born out of necessity from living
in such a cold, inhospitable country.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:08.110
And although the terrain is inhospitable,
the people are not and their respect and trust

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:14.552
of one-another is what makes Iceland the most
peaceful country in the world.

00:10:14.552 --> 00:10:21.260
The average homicides per year in the US is
15,000, the average homicides per year in

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:30.670
Iceland is one, just one and that truly is
something to be proud of.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:43.190
Thanks for watching.

